From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jinyu Meng <megabitsenmzq@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Allow portrait 4K decoding

The 2304-pixel height limit rejects portrait video even when its frame
size is within the 4K budget already accepted in landscape orientation.
Buffer sizes and codec registers are derived from the negotiated width
and height, so allow the same 4096-pixel maximum in both dimensions.
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 #define CEDRUS_MIN_WIDTH	16U
 #define CEDRUS_MIN_HEIGHT	16U
 #define CEDRUS_MAX_WIDTH	4096U
-#define CEDRUS_MAX_HEIGHT	2304U
+#define CEDRUS_MAX_HEIGHT	4096U
 
 static struct cedrus_format cedrus_formats[] = {
 	{
-- 
